The Linux audio capture path here is ported from these Sunshine sources:

  src/platform/linux/audio.cpp
      The pa::server_t control layer (pa_mainloop/pa_context setup, the state
      callback, the thread running pa_mainloop_run, the teardown order), sink
      and default-sink queries, monitor-source resolution via
      pa_sink_info::monitor_source_name, and the pa_simple recording stream
      with its pa_sample_spec / pa_channel_map / pa_buffer_attr construction.

  src/audio.h and src/audio.cpp
      The blocking pull interface (Sunshine's mic_t::sample() and this
      library's weba_capture_read_frame()), the fixed frame size derived from
      the packet duration, the 48 kHz float32 format, the bounded frame queue
      with drop-oldest overflow, and the reinit-on-failure retry behaviour.

  src/platform/linux/pipewire.cpp
      Reference for the control layer's threading and teardown patterns.

No Sunshine source file was copied wholesale. What was carried over is the
architecture and the libpulse API usage; Sunshine's infrastructure dependencies
(boost.log, safe::alarm_raw_t, safe::event_t, util::safe_ptr, util::fail_guard)
were replaced by src/primitives.h, and the public interface here is a pure C ABI
rather than Sunshine's C++ mic_t / audio_control_t class hierarchy.

Note that Sunshine's audio files carry no per-file copyright headers, so there
were no per-file notices to preserve. The project-level attribution above is
made under GPL-3.0 section 5(a).

See README.md for the list of deliberate differences from Sunshine.
